#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_document_l10n_mx_edi
msgid ""
"====================\n"
"CFDI file management\n"
"====================\n"
"\n"
"Pulls the company's CFDIs down from the SAT, files them as Documents, and\n"
"turns the ones that are vendor bills into ``account.move`` records.\n"
"\n"
"Everything here hangs off one asymmetry: the SAT is the authority on which\n"
"CFDIs exist, and Odoo is the authority on which of them have been accounted\n"
"for. The module's job is to keep those two in step without ever creating a\n"
"bill twice.\n"
"\n"
"The path a CFDI takes\n"
"=====================\n"
"\n"
"::\n"
"\n"
"    SAT (portal or web service)\n"
"      └─ l10n_mx_edi.session          one download request, one date range\n"
"           └─ ZIP of XML files\n"
"                └─ document.document one per CFDI, filed and tagged by content\n"
"                     └─ wizard        create a bill, or attach to an existing one\n"
"                          └─ account.move\n"
"\n"
"A session is the unit of work: it holds the request, its state, the package\n"
"the SAT produced, and the documents that came out of it. The daily cron\n"
"(``_cron_sync_with_sat``) creates a session for the current month and walks\n"
"it through request → verify → download for every company with a valid FIEL.\n"
"\n"
"Documents are filed by what the CFDI says, not by how it arrived: the\n"
"receptor RFC picks the company, the emisor RFC picks the Received or Issued\n"
"folder, and the stamp date supplies the year and month tags.\n"
"\n"
"Two transports, one contract\n"
"============================\n"
"\n"
"The SAT's mass-download SOAP service is not reliably available, so this fork\n"
"also drives the SAT portal through a self-hosted Playwright service. Both\n"
"speak the same three operations and return the same dict shapes, which is\n"
"what lets ``l10n_mx_edi.session`` treat them interchangeably.\n"
"\n"
"=============  ==================================  ===============================\n"
"\\              ``SatSoapClient``                   ``SatPortalClient``\n"
"=============  ==================================  ===============================\n"
"Transport      SOAP + WS-Security, RSA-SHA1        JSON over HTTP\n"
"Endpoint       ``*.clouda.sat.gob.mx``             the ``service_sat_portal`` record\n"
"Needs a token  yes, 300 s                          no\n"
"=============  ==================================  ===============================\n"
"\n"
"RSA-SHA1 is mandated by the SAT specification, not chosen.\n"
"\n"
"Both go out over ``integration``'s shared client rather than calling\n"
"``requests`` directly, so every SAT call leaves an ``integration.exchange`` row.\n"
"\"Did we ask the SAT for that package, and what did it say\" is a question a\n"
"fiscal integration has to answer from the database. Tests that stand in for\n"
"the network therefore patch ``requests.Session.request``, not\n"
"``requests.post``.\n"
"\n"
"``request_mode`` on the session picks one. Left unset, it tries the portal\n"
"and falls back to the web service.\n"
"\n"
"The date range is assumed to be read in Mexico City time\n"
"--------------------------------------------------------\n"
"\n"
"**Working assumption, not a verified fact.** ``FechaInicial`` and ``FechaFinal``\n"
"are ``xs:dateTime`` in the SAT's schema, which permits either an offset or a\n"
"naive local reading, and the SAT does not say which it takes. We assume it reads\n"
"them as **America/Mexico_City**, which since October 2022 is a fixed UTC-6 with\n"
"no daylight saving.\n"
"\n"
"What follows from that assumption is a six-hour hole, because the session stores\n"
"UTC and sends it verbatim. ``_generate_time_blocks`` builds a window of\n"
"00:00:00 to 23:59:59 Mexico, converts it to UTC, and the SAT is then handed:\n"
"\n"
"===================  ==========================  ==========================\n"
"\\                    stored and sent (UTC)       read as Mexico, per above\n"
"===================  ==========================  ==========================\n"
"``date_from``        ``2026-03-01 06:00:00``     01 Mar 06:00 local\n"
"``date_to``          ``2026-03-21 05:59:59``     21 Mar 05:59 local\n"
"===================  ==========================  ==========================\n"
"\n"
"So the intended window starts six hours late and ends six hours late: CFDIs from\n"
"**00:00 to 06:00 on the first of the month are never asked for**, by that session\n"
"or any later one, because every session for that month carries the same\n"
"``date_from``. The tail is merely redundant, since the next month's window\n"
"re-covers it; the head is a permanent gap.\n"
"\n"
"Under the other reading — the SAT parses the value as UTC — the window is exactly\n"
"right and nothing is missing. **The two readings are not distinguishable from the\n"
"data we have**, which is why this is written down rather than acted on:\n"
"``l10n_mx_edi_stamp_date`` holds ``FechaTimbrado`` verbatim and is therefore\n"
"local while the window is UTC, the SAT filters on emission date rather than the\n"
"stamp, and every window in the August 2026 production backup begins on a holiday\n"
"or a Sunday, so no CFDI sits near a boundary to show which way it fell.\n"
"\n"
"To settle it, compare a window that starts on a busy weekday against the emission\n"
"dates of what came back. ``document.document.l10n_mx_edi_emission_date`` now\n"
"stores the issuer's ``Fecha`` beside ``l10n_mx_edi_stamp_date``, so that\n"
"comparison is available on any session downloaded from here on; existing rows\n"
"are backfilled the next time their common fields recompute.\n"
"\n"
"If the assumption holds, the fix is to send Mexico-local naive datetimes instead\n"
"of UTC; the stored values stay UTC, as everything else in Odoo expects. Both\n"
"drivers need it, not one: ``SatSoapClient.request_download`` sends\n"
"``FechaInicial``/``FechaFinal``, and ``SatPortalClient.request_download`` sends\n"
"``str(date_to)`` on the same UTC value to a service that types it into the SAT's\n"
"Mexico-local form.\n"
"\n"
"Turning a CFDI into a bill\n"
"==========================\n"
"\n"
"Only ``TipoDeComprobante`` **I** and **E** carry money. A payment complement\n"
"(P), a payroll receipt (N) and a delivery guide (T) are filed and tagged like\n"
"anything else, but the wizard will not offer to bill them — a Traslado states\n"
"``SubTotal`` 0, ``Total`` 0 and the currency ``XXX``. It can still be assigned\n"
"to a journal entry that already exists. Every line the wizard declines says\n"
"why, in its own column.\n"
"\n"
"**Taxes are matched structurally, not by name.** ``account.tax.name`` is a\n"
"translated field, so matching on it made a fiscal amount depend on a ``.po``\n"
"file: where a Spanish name is missing, \"VAT 16.0%\" does not contain \"IVA\", and\n"
"on the chart Odoo itself ships — ``16%``, ``4% WH``, ``10.67% WH L`` — nothing\n"
"matched at all. ``_find_tax`` narrows on ``l10n_mx_tax_type``, which is the\n"
"same fact the CFDI states in its ``Impuesto`` code, together with the rate,\n"
"the factor type and the tax use. The name only breaks a tie, because several\n"
"taxes in the MX chart differ solely in deductibility, which no CFDI expresses.\n"
"When the tie cannot be broken it takes the first and logs the alternatives.\n"
"\n"
"A chart that leaves ``l10n_mx_tax_type`` unset falls back to the old\n"
"name-based search, so nothing that used to resolve stops resolving.\n"
"\n"
"Fuel is two lines, always: the litres at their own price, and the IEPS. The\n"
"excise has to be separate because ``Importe`` is the base *before* it while\n"
"the IVA above it is charged on base + IEPS — splitting them is what makes the\n"
"lines add up to the total the CFDI declares.\n"
"\n"
"Duplicate detection\n"
"===================\n"
"\n"
"The one invariant worth stating plainly: **a CFDI is identified by its folio\n"
"fiscal and nothing else.**\n"
"\n"
"``_get_duplicate_cfdi`` compares UUIDs, never filenames. The same package\n"
"downloaded twice, an overlapping date range, a manual upload of files\n"
"already fetched by the cron — all of these are normal, and none of them may\n"
"produce a second document or a second bill. Three layers enforce it: the ZIP\n"
"extraction skips known UUIDs, ``document.document.create()`` skips them\n"
"again, and ``account.move._post()`` refuses to post a second bill claiming a\n"
"UUID already on file.\n"
"\n"
"Note that ``create()`` therefore returns fewer records than it was given\n"
"when it skips one. That is a deliberate deviation from the ORM contract, and\n"
"it is documented on the method.\n"
"\n"
"Credentials\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"``l10n_mx_edi.esignature`` holds the FIEL: certificate, private key and\n"
"passphrase. Those three fields are readable only by\n"
"``group_documents_l10n_mx_edi_manager``; the download flow reaches them\n"
"through ``get_cert_data()`` / ``get_pk_data()``, which sudo deliberately so\n"
"that an operator can run a download without being able to read the key over\n"
"RPC.\n"
"\n"
"Validity is stored and compared in UTC. The certificate's own window is the\n"
"authority — ``get_valid_esignature()`` returns the first signature that\n"
"covers the current instant, or an empty recordset.\n"
"\n"
"Field-level groups govern who may *read* the key through Odoo. What a database\n"
"dump, a replica or a backup carries is a different question, answered by\n"
"``documents_l10n_mx_edi_encryption``: install it and the three secrets become\n"
"Fernet-encrypted columns, with the field names and the whole flow unchanged.\n"
"\n"
"It ships separately because the encryption mixin hard-requires\n"
"``ODOO_API_ENCRYPTION_KEY``, and a deployment that has not provisioned a Fernet\n"
"key keeps working exactly as before by not installing it. Its install refuses,\n"
"touching nothing, when there are signatures to migrate and no key.\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"=========================  ====================================================  =========\n"
"Setting                    Key                                                   Default\n"
"=========================  ====================================================  =========\n"
"SAT validation batch size  ``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_batch_size``               50\n"
"Review period, days        ``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_status_max_days``          60\n"
"Max verification attempts  ``document_l10n_mx_edi.default_max_verify_cfdi``      200\n"
"Verification deadline, h   ``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_verify_deadline_hours``    72\n"
"SOAP request timeout, s    ``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_soap_request_timeout``     180\n"
"SOAP download timeout, s   ``document_l10n_mx_edi.sat_soap_download_timeout``    420\n"
"=========================  ====================================================  =========\n"
"\n"
"The review period is counted in **calendar** days, not working days.\n"
"\n"
"The portal's address and timeout are **not** system parameters. They live on\n"
"the ``service_sat_portal`` record (Settings → Technical → API → Services), as\n"
"``endpoint_url`` and ``timeout_read``, because that is the record\n"
"``integration`` bills the call against. They used to be\n"
"``cfdi_downloader.ec2.url`` / ``.timeout``; a hook adopts those on upgrade, so\n"
"an existing deployment keeps its address.\n"
"\n"
"Set the company's e-signature and CFDI folder under\n"
"Settings → Documents → Mexican Electronic Documents.\n"
"\n"
"Crons\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"* **Auto Import CFDI SAT** — daily; creates and advances sessions per company.\n"
"* **Update SAT status (documents)** — daily; re-checks the SAT status of\n"
"  stamped documents not yet linked to a bill, oldest first, in batches.\n"
"\n"
"Optional integrations\n"
"=====================\n"
"\n"
"* **Fuel statements.** A CFDI carrying an ``EstadoDeCuentaCombustible12``\n"
"  complemento needs ``asset_ledger`` for the vehicle logs. It is not a\n"
"  declared dependency; the import refuses with a message naming the module.\n"
"* **Utility bills.** CFE bills carry meter readings in a non-standard\n"
"  addenda. ``cfe_addenda_parser`` (XML) and ``cfe_pdf_parser`` (PDF\n"
"  fallback) extract them and hand the result to the ``utility_bill``\n"
"  framework. Both are Odoo-free and unit-testable on fixtures.\n"
"\n"
"When it stops downloading\n"
"=========================\n"
"\n"
"Every timeout in this path is short somewhere it should not be, and the SAT is\n"
"slow in a way that reads as \"broken\" rather than \"slow\". Before diagnosing\n"
"anything else, read ``doc/2026-09-03-sat-download-outage.rst``: it records five\n"
"defects of exactly that shape, what each looked like from the outside, and the\n"
"one that silently drops a healthy session out of its own retry cycle.\n"
"\n"
"Two things it will save you from concluding. A climbing ``count_verify`` with an\n"
"unmoving ``request_state`` is not \"the SAT is preparing the package\" -- it is\n"
"just as likely that no round trip ever completed. And the browser half of this\n"
"lives in ``/opt/cfdi_downloader``, outside any repository, so a fix there leaves\n"
"no trace in ``git log``.\n"
"\n"
"Tests\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"::\n"
"\n"
"    odoo-bin -c <conf> -d <db> -u documents_l10n_mx_edi \\\n"
"        --test-tags /document_l10n_mx_edi --stop-after-init\n"
"\n"
"Two suites carry most of the weight:\n"
"\n"
"* ``test_cfdi_import_flow.py`` walks bytes → document → wizard → posted\n"
"  move, plus the awkward packages: duplicates, a bad currency among good\n"
"  files, a payment complement, a SAT manifest.\n"
"* ``test_audit_findings.py`` pins the findings of the 2026-08 audit. Its\n"
"  ``test_rejected_*`` cases record theories that turned out **not** to be\n"
"  defects, so they are not re-derived.\n"
"\n"
"The parser suites run against anonymized fixtures in ``tests/fixtures/`` and\n"
"need no database.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_account_move_template
msgid ""
"=====================\n"
"Account Move Template\n"
"=====================\n"
"\n"
".. |badge1| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/maturity-Production%2FStable-green.png\n"
"    :target: https://odoo-community.org/page/development-status\n"
"    :alt: Production/Stable\n"
".. |badge2| image:: https://img.shields.io/badge/licence-AGPL--3-blue.png\n"
"    :target: http://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0-standalone.html\n"
"    :alt: License: AGPL-3\n"
"\n"
"|badge1| |badge2|\n"
"\n"
"Templates for the documents AgroMarin issues over and over: journal entries,\n"
"vendor bills, customer invoices, credit notes and outbound payments. A template\n"
"holds the journal, the partner, the accounts and the products; running it opens\n"
"a wizard that asks for the few things that change -- a date, an amount, a\n"
"partner -- and creates the document.\n"
"\n"
"This module began as ``account_move_template`` from\n"
"`OCA/account-financial-tools <https://github.com/OCA/account-financial-tools>`_\n"
"and has since diverged: the upstream features built on ``opt_account_id``, an\n"
"overwrite dictionary and Python-computed amounts are **not** present here, and\n"
"everything below was added for this fork. It is no longer generated by\n"
"``oca-gen-addon-readme``; edit this file directly.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"**Journal and account codes.** A template names its journal by *code*, not by\n"
"id, and each line names its account by *code prefix*. Both resolve at run time,\n"
"in the company the run belongs to, so one template serves every company that\n"
"uses the same chart of accounts and the same journal codes. The ``Journal`` and\n"
"``Account`` pickers next to them show what the stored code currently resolves\n"
"to; picking one fills the code.\n"
"\n"
"**Payment product families.** Set ``Payment family`` (technical name\n"
"``payment_category_code``) on a product category -- ``AGROQUIMICOS``, ``PAPAS``\n"
"-- to tag it as part of a family. Subcategories inherit the tag unless they\n"
"carry one of their own, which splits them off into their own family. A template\n"
"that ticks ``Take the product from the payment's category`` then draws its\n"
"product from whichever family the run names.\n"
"\n"
"Two system parameters tune the draw:\n"
"\n"
"``account_move_template.payment_min_price``\n"
"   A price floor. Products priced below it are never drawn, which keeps\n"
"   catalogue placeholders priced at a token amount out of stamped documents.\n"
"   Defaults to no floor.\n"
"\n"
"``account_move_template.random_product_supplier_tax_id``\n"
"   The id of the supplier tax that a template line with a ``Product category``\n"
"   filters on. Required by that path; a run raises if it is unset.\n"
"\n"
"**Pinning a product.** Set ``Payment Product`` on one category of a family when\n"
"that family always bills the same article. The pin is used verbatim instead of\n"
"a draw, so a sibling product can never end up on a stamped CFDI. Only one\n"
"category per family may pin a product.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"Journal entry templates\n"
"-----------------------\n"
"\n"
"Give the template a journal code, ``Journal Entry`` as the move type, and one\n"
"line per journal item with an account prefix and a balance. Balances must sum\n"
"to zero, as on any entry. Run it from the ``Use Template`` button on the\n"
"template, or from ``Accounting > Create Entry from Template``.\n"
"\n"
"Invoice and bill templates\n"
"--------------------------\n"
"\n"
"Pick ``Vendor Bill``, ``Customer Invoice`` or either credit note. Lines carry a\n"
"product or a product category, a quantity, a unit price, taxes and an optional\n"
"discount. A line whose product is left to a category draws one at run time.\n"
"\n"
"The wizard's ``Amount`` is the **total of the document**. It is distributed\n"
"across the product lines, with the rounding residue on the last one, so\n"
"``amount_untaxed`` always equals what was typed. Each line decides how it\n"
"spends its share through ``Distribution method``:\n"
"\n"
"``Collapse (one line, full amount)``\n"
"   One line, quantity 1, priced at the share. Use it for discounts, fees and\n"
"   single-item credit notes, where the template's own unit price is only a\n"
"   placeholder.\n"
"\n"
"``Split (decompose into units of price_unit)``\n"
"   As many whole units at the template's unit price as the share pays for, plus\n"
"   one adjustment line for the remainder. The adjustment carries the same taxes\n"
"   as the units it completes. Use it for bills expressed as \"N units at X\".\n"
"\n"
"Sections and notes\n"
"------------------\n"
"\n"
"A line can be a ``Section`` or a ``Note`` instead of a product. They carry no\n"
"accounting value, take no share of the amount, and are written to the generated\n"
"document as display lines in sequence with the product lines around them.\n"
"\n"
"Payment templates\n"
"-----------------\n"
"\n"
"Tick ``Is payment``, choose the payment type and partner type, and give the\n"
"template a bank journal code. Template lines are not used. The wizard's\n"
"``Payment Amount`` is required, and the payment is returned **in draft** --\n"
"posting is left to whoever asked for it.\n"
"\n"
"Secondary partner\n"
"-----------------\n"
"\n"
"A run can carry a ``diff_partner_id``: the party a discount is applied to, named\n"
"when the payment was requested. It is informational by default, so the\n"
"accounting owner stays on the document. Tick ``Issue to the secondary partner``\n"
"on a template to have that template's documents issued to it instead. Leave it\n"
"off wherever the owner has to stay on the document -- the customer invoice of a\n"
"discount run is one of those.\n"
"\n"
"Multi-company\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"A template may carry a company or leave it empty. An empty company means the\n"
"template is shared, and its journal code is validated against the companies the\n"
"user can act for. The run itself always resolves one company -- the wizard's\n"
"``multicompany_id`` if given, else the template's, else the automation runtime's,\n"
"else the active one -- and resolves the journal and the accounts inside it.\n"
"\n"
"Known issues\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"* The name of an archived template stays reserved: a new template cannot reuse\n"
"  it until the archived row is deleted. This follows the framework default for\n"
"  catalog-style name indexes.\n"
"\n"
"Integrations\n"
"============\n"
"\n"
"``automation_account``\n"
"   Calls the wizard from a server action, passing the runtime's partner, date,\n"
"   amount, secondary partner, target company and payment family. It takes an\n"
"   ``auto_post`` flag and posts the result itself.\n"
"\n"
"``l10n_mx_edi_account_move_template``\n"
"   Adds the CFDI usage code and payment method to the wizard and forwards them\n"
"   to the generated move.\n"
"\n"
"``account_move_template_purchase``\n"
"   Links a template to a purchase bill match.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"-------\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
"* Akretion\n"
"* Odoo Community Association (OCA)\n"
msgstr ""

