#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_planning_mrp
msgid ""
"======================\n"
"Planning Manufacturing\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"This module integrates Odoo's Planning and Manufacturing modules to provide\n"
"comprehensive production planning and scheduling capabilities. It extends\n"
"planning slots with manufacturing-specific fields and adds cancellation\n"
"workflow with reason tracking.\n"
"\n"
"The module provides:\n"
"\n"
"* **Manufacturing Planning Integration**: Link planning slots to workcenters, work orders, and production orders\n"
"* **Cancellation Management**: Structured cancellation process with reasons and employee notifications\n"
"* **Real-time Visibility**: Active planning slot counters on workcenter views\n"
"* **Advanced Filtering**: Search and group planning slots by manufacturing criteria\n"
"* **Audit Trail**: Complete tracking of planning changes and cancellations\n"
"\n"
"This integration enables manufacturing teams to efficiently plan production\n"
"schedules, manage resource allocation, and maintain transparency in planning\n"
"operations with full traceability.\n"
"\n"
"Access model\n"
"------------\n"
"\n"
"The module adds two groups under the Manufacturing privilege, both of which\n"
"widen what core Planning grants:\n"
"\n"
"* **Planning Manufacturing User** implies ``planning.group_planning_user`` and\n"
"  ``mrp.group_mrp_user``. Core Planning gives a planning user read-only access\n"
"  to shifts; this group may also create and edit them, which is the point of\n"
"  the module - manufacturing staff build their own production shifts. It may\n"
"  not delete them.\n"
"* **Planning Manufacturing Manager** implies the user group above plus\n"
"  ``planning.group_planning_manager`` and ``mrp.group_mrp_manager``, and may\n"
"  delete shifts.\n"
"\n"
"Publishing a shift is a planning-manager action: the Publish and Send buttons\n"
"and the status bar are gated on ``planning.group_planning_manager``, so a\n"
"manufacturing user builds a schedule and a planning manager releases it. Note\n"
"that this is a gate in the views, not a permission - the write itself is\n"
"allowed, so the two-step handoff is a convention rather than something the\n"
"server enforces.\n"
"\n"
"Neither group is granted to anyone by default; both must be assigned\n"
"deliberately.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"To use this module, you need to:\n"
"\n"
"#. Go to Manufacturing > Planning > Schedule\n"
"#. Create planning slots and link them to:\n"
"\n"
"   * **Workcenters**: Select the manufacturing workcenter\n"
"   * **Work Orders**: Link to specific manufacturing work orders\n"
"   * **Production Orders**: Associate with production orders\n"
"   * **Products**: Specify products to manufacture\n"
"\n"
"#. Configure default settings:\n"
"\n"
"   * Go to Settings > General Settings > Planning Integration\n"
"   * Set the **Default Manufacturing Planning Project** for automatic assignment\n"
"\n"
"#. Manage cancellations:\n"
"\n"
"   * Use the **Cancel Shift** button on published planning slots\n"
"   * Select a **Cancellation Reason** from predefined options\n"
"   * Optionally notify assigned employees\n"
"   * View cancellation history in the planning slot form\n"
"\n"
"#. Monitor planning activity:\n"
"\n"
"   * View **Active Planning Slot Count** on workcenter kanban cards\n"
"   * Access planning schedules directly from workcenter views\n"
"   * Use advanced filters to group by workcenter, product, or work order\n"
"\n"
"The module provides several planning views:\n"
"\n"
"* **By Resource**: Plan by employee/resource assignments\n"
"* **By Role**: Plan by employee roles and skills\n"
"* **By Workcenter**: Plan by manufacturing workcenters\n"
"* **By Product**: Plan by products to manufacture\n"
"\n"
"**Cancellation Reasons**: The module includes predefined cancellation reasons\n"
"(Equipment Failure, Material Shortage, Employee Absence, Customer Request,\n"
"Maintenance Required) which can be customized in Planning > Configuration >\n"
"Cancellation Reasons.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin/issues>`_.\n"
"In case of trouble, please check there if your issue has already been reported.\n"
"If you spotted it first, help us to smash it by providing a detailed and welcomed\n"
"`feedback <https://github.com/Agro-Marin/agromarin/issues/new?body=module:%20planning_mrp%0Aversion:%2019.0%0A%0A**Steps%20to%20reproduce**%0A-%20...%0A%0A**Current%20behavior**%0A%0A**Expected%20behavior**>`_.\n"
"\n"
"Do not contact contributors directly about support or help with technical issues.\n"
"\n"
"Credits\n"
"=======\n"
"\n"
"Authors\n"
"~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"* AgroMarin\n"
"\n"
"Contributors\n"
"~~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"* Luis Marin <luis.marin@agromarin.mx>\n"
"\n"
"Maintainers\n"
"~~~~~~~~~~~\n"
"\n"
"This module is maintained by AgroMarin.\n"
"\n"
".. image:: https://www.agromarin.mx/logo.png\n"
"   :alt: AgroMarin\n"
"   :target: https://www.agromarin.mx\n"
"\n"
"AgroMarin is a company specialized in agricultural ERP solutions based on Odoo.\n"
"\n"
"You are welcome to contribute. To learn how please visit https://www.agromarin.mx.\n"
msgstr ""

#. module: base
#: model:ir.module.module,description:base.module_telegram_bot_approval
msgid ""
"======================\n"
"Telegram Bot Approval\n"
"======================\n"
"\n"
"This module adds base fields to approval.request for storing\n"
"data received from Telegram bot interactions.\n"
"\n"
"**Table of contents**\n"
"\n"
".. contents::\n"
"   :local:\n"
"\n"
"Features\n"
"========\n"
"\n"
"* ``telegram_data``: JSON field for storing payment details from Telegram\n"
"* ``telegram_data_formatted``: Computed HTML field for displaying data in Odoo\n"
"\n"
"Configuration\n"
"=============\n"
"\n"
"No specific configuration is required.\n"
"\n"
"Usage\n"
"=====\n"
"\n"
"This module provides the base data structure for Telegram approval requests.\n"
"\n"
"For full Telegram payment approval functionality (commands, workflow, etc.),\n"
"install ``telegram_bot_approval_automation_account``.\n"
"\n"
"Bug Tracker\n"
"===========\n"
"\n"
"Bugs are tracked on `GitHub Issues <https://github.com/AgroMarin/agromarin-addons/issues>`_.\n"
